{"name":"Heirloom Shade","hex":"#dcd8d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heirloom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A valued possession that has been passed down through the generations.","An old crop variety that has been passed down through generations of farmers by seed saving and cultivation, in contrast to modern cultivars used in large-scale agriculture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heirloom"},{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heirloom","blocks":[{"text":"In popular usage, an heirloom is something that has been passed down for generations through family members. Examples are a family Bible, antiques, weapons or jewellery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Soldier%27s_return.jpg/330px-Soldier%27s_return.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heirloom","wikidata":"Q16842191"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"